"'''Rolling in the Deep'''" is a song by English singer-songwriter [[Adele]] from her second studio album, ''[[21 (Adele album)|21]]'' (2011). It is the [[lead single]] and opening track on the album. The song was written by Adele and [[Paul Epworth]]. The singer herself describes it as a "dark blues-y gospel disco tune".<ref name="Adele"/> In 2011, it was reportedly the biggest [[crossover hit]] in the United States since 1985; "Rolling in the Deep" gained radio airplay from many different radio formats.<ref>{{Cite magazine|last=Trust|first=Gary|date=14 July 2011|title=Adele's 'Rolling in the Deep' Is The Biggest Crossover Song of Past 25 Years|url=http://www.billboard.biz/bbbiz/industry/record-labels/adele-s-rolling-in-the-deep-is-the-biggest-1005277742.story|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110717132028/http://www.billboard.biz/bbbiz/industry/record-labels/adele-s-rolling-in-the-deep-is-the-biggest-1005277742.story|archive-date=17 July 2011|access-date=3 March 2021|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|language=en}}</ref> It was released on 29 November 2010 as the lead single from ''21'' in digital download format. The lyrics describe the emotions of a scorned lover. 

"Rolling in the Deep" received widespread critical acclaim with praise drawn towards the song's production, its lyrics, and Adele's vocal performance. It represented a commercial breakthrough for Adele, propelling her to global superstardom. The song topped the charts in twelve countries and reached the top 10 in over twenty territories. It was Adele's first number-one song in the United States, reaching the top spot on many [[Billboard charts|''Billboard'' charts]], including the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] where it was number one for seven weeks. By February 2012, "Rolling in the Deep" had sold over 8.7 million copies in the United States, making it the best-selling digital song by a female artist in the US,<ref name=ChartWatch>{{cite web |last=Grein |first=Paul |url=http://music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart-watch/week-ending-april-15-2012-songs-gotye-beats-220532819.html |title=Week Ending April 15, 2012. Songs: Gotye Beats Bieber &#124; Chart Watch (NEW) – Yahoo! Music |publisher=Music.yahoo.com |date=18 April 2012 |access-date=11 June 2012 |archive-date=28 May 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120528195139/http://music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart-watch/week-ending-april-15-2012-songs-gotye-beats-220532819.html |url-status=live }}</ref> the second-best-selling digital song in the US and Adele's best-selling single outside her native country, topping her previous best-selling "[[Chasing Pavements]]". Worldwide, it was the fifth-best-selling digital single of 2011 with sales of 8.2 million copies.<ref>{{cite web|title=IFPI DIGITAL MUSIC REPORT 2012 – KEY FACTS AND FIGURES |url=http://ifpi.com/content/library/DMR2012_key_facts_and_figures.pdf |publisher=[[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry]] |access-date=23 January 2012 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121030053448/http://ifpi.com/content/library/DMR2012_key_facts_and_figures.pdf |archive-date=30 October 2012 }}</ref> {{As of|2019}}, with sales of over 20.6 million copies worldwide, "Rolling in the Deep" is one of the [[List of best-selling singles|best-selling digital singles of all-time]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20130104005149/en/Nielsen-Company-Billboard%E2%80%99s-2012-Music-Industry-Report|title=The Nielsen Company & Billboard's 2012 Music Industry Report|publisher=[[Business Wire]]|work=[[Nielsen Company]]|date=4 January 2013|access-date=14 February 2013|archive-date=12 January 2013|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130112121109/http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20130104005149/en/Nielsen-Company-Billboard%E2%80%99s-2012-Music-Industry-Report|url-status=live}}
