Its music video received a leading seven nominations at the [[2011 MTV Video Music Awards]], including for [[MTV Video Music Award for Video of the Year|Video of the Year]], and won three other awards: [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Editing|Best Editing]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Cinematography|Best Cinematography]] and [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Art Direction|Best Art Direction]].<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/469155/katy-perry-adele-kanye-west-lead-2011-mtv-vma-nominees|title=Katy Perry, Adele, Kanye West Lead 2011 MTV VMA Nominees|magazine=Billboard|publisher=Prometheus Global Media|first=Phil|last=Gallo|location=Los Angeles|date=20 July 2011|access-date=10 December 2011}}</ref><ref name="mtv">{{cite web|title=2011 MTV Video Music Awards Winners|url=http://www.mtv.com/ontv/vma/2011/winners.jhtml|publisher=MTV. MTV Networks|access-date=31 August 2011|date=28 August 2011|archive-date=22 June 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120622132012/http://www.mtv.com/ontv/vma/2011/winners.jhtml|url-status=dead}}</ref> "Rolling in the Deep" was also the [[Billboard Year End|''Billboard'' Year End]] Hot 100 Number One Single of 2011. At the [[54th Annual Grammy Awards]], it won awards for [[Grammy Award for Record of the Year|Record of the Year]], [[Grammy Award for Song of the Year|Song of the Year]], and [[Grammy Award for Best Short Form Music Video|Best Short Form Music Video]].<ref>{{cite magazine|title=The Grammys: Adele, Kanye West Lead Nominations|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/events/grammys/464897/the-grammys-adele-kanye-west-lead-nominations|first1=David|last1=Greenwald|first2=Marc|last2=Schneider|magazine=Billboard|publisher=Prometheus Global Media|page=2|date=30 November 2011|access-date=10 December 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.grammy.com/nominees?year=2011&genre=All|title=54th Annual Grammy Awards|publisher=Grammy.com. [[National Academy of Recording Arts and Sciences]]|access-date=10 December 2011|archive-date=18 June 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120618002523/http://www.grammy.com/nominees?year=2011|url-status=live}}</ref> Various critics and music publications ranked it as the best song of the year on their end-of-year lists with ''[[Rolling Stone]]'' ranking it at No.&nbsp;8 spot on its list of "The 100 Greatest Songs of the 21st Century".<ref>{{cite magazine |first1=David |last1=Greenwald |last2=Schneider |first2=Marc |date=30 November 2011 |title=The 100 Greatest Songs of the Century − So Far |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/the-100-greatest-songs-of-the-century-so-far-666874/?list_page=2 |magazine=Rolling Stone |page=2 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220309214446/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/the-100-greatest-songs-of-the-century-so-far-666874/the-scientist-coldplay-666809 |archive-date=9 March 2022 |access-date=13 June 2022}}</ref> In 2021, the song was ranked at number 82 on the list of [[Rolling Stone's 500 Greatest Songs of All Time|''Rolling Stone''{{'}}s 500 Greatest Songs of All Time]].<ref>{{cite magazine |date=15 December 2021 |title=The 500 Greatest Songs of All Time |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/best-songs-of-all-time-1224767/adele-rolling-in-the-deep-2-1225256/ |url-status=live |magazine=Rolling Stone |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220614200030/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/best-songs-of-all-time-1224767/bob-dylan-blowin-in-the-wind-3-1225238/ |archive-date=14 June 2022 |access-date=14 June 2022}}</ref>

